  abstract[Elsevier]: We propose the measurement of the angular decay distribution of leptons from W-production at high- q T in p p collisions. The polar and azimuthal angles in the W rest frame can be reconstructed modulo a sign ambiguity in cos θ enabling the measurement of sic out of nine helicity cross sections σ α describing the most general decay distribution. We review the LO results of the nine helicity cross sections and present result of complete O( α s 2 ) next-to-leading (NLO) calculation of four parity conserving structure functions. We show that large deviations from the well-known (1+cos θ 2 ) distribution valid at low- q T are expected already at moderate transverse W-momentum ( q T ≈20GeV). The measurement of the sign of the “ T -odd” helicity cross sections will discriminate between V - A and V + A couplings of the W. We present detailed analytical formulas for all parton level cross sections and discuss the size of the NLO corrections for W + production at the Tevatron collider. It is shown that the measurement of σ A (originating from the parity violating part of the hadron tensor) provide clear constraints on the gluon structure function since it receives sizable contributions only from the qG initiated process.

